      "category": "correctness",
      "title": "Held report is still discarded on paths where no review replaces it",
      "description": "The discard now sits after the merge/no-source skips, but two later exits still abandon it with nothing taking its place: the empty-diff return at line 499-502 and the `result.error` return at line 520-524. In both cases `this.held` has already been set to `undefined` (and it is unrecoverable — `sendHeld` only reads `this.held`), so a failed or timed-out `runReview` on the fixing commit silently destroys the held findings.",
      "suggestion": "Consider moving the discard block below the empty-diff check and the `result.error` early return — e.g. just before `this.display(...)`/`this.report(...)` — so the hold is only superseded once a review has actually produced findings for the new commit.",
